<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Obwalden</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Obwalden is a canton of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a> south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-lucerne">Lake Lucerne</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarnen">Sarnen</a>. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nidwalden">Nidwalden</a> it formed Unterwalden, one of the three founding members of the Old Swiss Confederacy in 1291, and each half governed itself through its own assembly. The territory of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/engelberg">Engelberg</a> Abbey was added to Obwalden in 1815.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/obwalden.jpg" alt="Obwalden" width="320" height="264" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tschubby · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karte_Kanton_Obwalden_2010.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
